<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Control Instruments half year shr falls.</title>
<headline>Control Instruments half year shr falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     4.3	   vs 11.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 2.5	   vs 2.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.51	  vs 8.32</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   5.21	  vs 10.68</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.59	  vs 2.24</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   0.85	  vs 0.03</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    3.36	  vs 1.79</p>
<p>    Turnover		  119.48	vs 129.64</p>
<p>Div payable April 25</p>
<p>on register April 4</p>
<p>Full name: Control Instruments Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the fall in earnings mainly reflected abnormally high cellular phone sales in the corresponding period. Interest and depreciation costs were higher following the acquisition of Rhomberg-Brasler.</p>
<p>The company said earnings in the second half should at least equal earnings in the comparable year ago period.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
